    "summary": "rsync through 3.5.1 contains a denial of service vulnerability in the delta-transfer sender's...",
    "details": "rsync before 3.5.2 contains a denial of service vulnerability in the delta-transfer sender's `hash_search()` in match.c that allows malicious receivers to trigger unbounded strong-checksum work at consecutive offsets. Unauthenticated attackers pulling from a public daemon module can supply weak checksums colliding with consecutive rolling windows plus non-matching strong checksums, exhausting sender CPU across concurrent connections.",
    "severity": [
        {
